-- chem/sectorground.hypercubical — every neutral flux sector at a four-valent vertex holds the state with no flux at the
-- vertex itself. The magnetic operator's loops change only the innermost labels at the vertex and keep every
-- edge's flux to its neighbour (chem/magloop.hypercubical, word-keeps). A loop α_{e0} raised to the power −n_e moves the
-- innermost label of edge e from n_e to 0 and adds n_e to edge 0's; doing this for e = 1, 2, 3 leaves edge 0 with
-- n_0 + n_1 + n_2 + n_3, which is 0 at a neutral vertex. So from any flux pattern to the neighbours, with total
-- charge zero, a product of loops reaches innermost labels all 0 and leaves the pattern as it was. The electric
-- energy at the vertex is ½ |Σ_e n_e T_e|² over the innermost labels (chem/magnetic.hypercubical, tet-electric-triad), a
-- square, so it is never below 0 and is 0 there: the lowest energy in every neutral sector is 0, the same for every
-- flux pattern to the neighbours. Checked below on three patterns.
import "magloop.hypercubical"

